{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothRealLadder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothRealLadder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothVariableSplit","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Real.Irrational"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_le_rothBound_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_le_rothBound_witness","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L164-L193","doc":"**Non-vacuity of Roth's Lemma at `m = 2`** — the arity §13 actually needs (`m ≥ 2`).\n\n`p = q = 1` (so `t = 1`), `F = 10`, `d ≡ 1`, `H ≡ 1024`, `a = 1`, `A = 1`, `κ ≡ 1024`.\n\n⚠ The heights **cannot** be small.  Clause 3 forces `2^F ≤ K₁` with `q·(m−1)m(2m+1) ≤ F·p`, so\nat `m = 2` the floor is `2^{10} = 1024`.  Every other witness in this arc got away with `H = 2`;\nthis is the one place where clause 3 bites, and exhibiting it is the point — a satisfiability\nclaim about `Γ_m` that quietly used `H = 2` would be about a different hypothesis.\n\n⚠ `t = 1` makes the bound itself weak (`Θ ≤ c₂ = 5`).  That is a limitation of *this witness*,\nnot of the theorem: what it establishes is that the hypothesis stack is satisfiable at `m ≥ 2`,\nso the theorem is not vacuous where §13 lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_le_rothBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_le_rothBound","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L135-L162","doc":"**Roth's Lemma (§14).**  If `a; r₁,…,r_m; H₁,…,H_m` has property `Γ_m` with `t = p/q`, then\nevery `A ∈ R(a;r)` has index at most `c_m·t^{2^{−(m−1)}}` at every `κ ∈ Q(H)`, where\n`c_m = 2^{m+1} − 3`.\n\nThe conclusion is root-free: `Θ^{2^{m−1}} ≤ c_m^{2^{m−1}}·t`.  ⚠ `Θ` is existential because it\nis `Θ_m` — the bound is uniform over `R(a;r) × Q(H)`, which is stronger than a bound depending\non `A` and `κ`, and is what §12 invokes when it recurses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothLemmaTheta_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothLemmaTheta_all","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L125-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothLemmaTheta_succ'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothLemmaTheta_succ'","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L113-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothBound_succ_of_lemma4'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothBound_succ_of_lemma4'","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L61-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sqrtIter_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sqrtIter_pow","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L54-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sqrtIter_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sqrtIter_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L44-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sqrtIter_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sqrtIter_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothRealLadder.lean#L39-L42","signatureChunk":0}]}